./build
./benchmarks
!./benchmarks/OOPSLA26
./demo

# .git (hundreds of MB of history) and backup/ (old PDFs, multiple GB) were
# previously being copied into every image via `COPY . .` — neither is needed
# to build or run autoq. This was the actual source of image bloat.
.git
./backup

# Documentation-only image assets, not needed to build/run.
./algorithms

# Legacy pre-MIT-relicensing artifacts (see AE/README.md "Licensing"): not on
# the code path exercised by this artifact, no need to ship them in the image.
./vata
./COPYING

# Stale generated tables from a native (non-Docker) run, regenerated fresh by
# run.sh inside the container anyway.
AE/table1.csv
AE/table2.csv

# Stale reference material from a prior CAV26 packaging run — not part of
# the OOPSLA26 AE artifact, kept on disk locally but must not enter any image.
./AE
!./AE/run.sh
!./AE/reusable-example
!./AE/scripts